<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM-DESIGN-ACK-CONSOLIDATION-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM-DESIGN-ACK-CONSOLIDATION-001" ;
  triage:title "Ack is internally send-with-a-flag but graft/trait code still carries a separate acknowledge_message path instead of collapsing to send_message" ;
  triage:description "AckRequest::into_write_request() (crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs) already proves acknowledgement is just a SendRequest with acknowledges_message_id set and requires_ack: false -- there is no independent ack semantics at the storage/write layer. Despite that, AtmGraftClient (crates/atm-core/src/graft.rs) still exposes acknowledge_message() as a fully separate trait method taking a distinct AckRequest type rather than collapsing internally to send_message() with the ack fields set. Scope note (user-clarified): the `atm ack` CLI subcommand itself is fine and stays as-is (crates/atm/src/commands/ack.rs, wired via crates/atm/src/commands/mod.rs is NOT part of this finding -- kept only as an occurrence reference for where AckRequest is constructed before entering the write path). The actual defect is internal-only: the trait/client/PyO3 layers (AtmGraftClient::acknowledge_message, GraftClient's impl, PyGraftSession::acknowledge) should not carry a second write method distinct from send_message -- they should call through the same send path with the ack fields populated, removing the duplicate internal call path. Not a regression and not blocking AM's deletion-only exit gate (AM.6 already closed); this is new internal API-shape scope, so it needs a dedicated fix/sprint decision rather than folding into the current PR #840 phase-end fix batch." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "api-design" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "single-branch" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-12T03:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Superseded the prior 'deferred' disposition: the feature/hermes-atm-native-ack merge (commit 51f92a5c, reviewed in QA-GRAFT-RECONNECT-2/3 on PR #854, merged to integrate/phase-am @3c60310c) resolves this at the code level. AtmGraftClient (crates/atm-core/src/graft.rs) no longer defines acknowledge_message() -- it exposes only send_message/read_message/list_messages (confirmed via direct grep, zero matches on this branch). AckRequest::into_write_request() (crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs) remains the sole conversion path, now also reused by PyGraftSession::send/send_tool's optional acknowledges_message_id field. An existing architecture test (crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs) forbids GraftClient from exposing acknowledge_message, and a new test asserts PyGraftSession has no `acknowledge` attribute. Independently confirmed by 3 reviewers (ruthless-boundary-qa, arch-qa, req-qa) across QA-GRAFT-RECONNECT-2 and -3. The atm ack CLI subcommand (o3/o4) was never part of this finding's actual scope, per the original description." ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-11T15:05:06Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AM-PHASEEND ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-11T15:05:06Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
